==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|talkere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|talk|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-talker.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːkə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[talk]]s, especially one who gives a [[speech]], or is [[loquacious]] or [[garrulous]].
#: {{ux|en|What this country needs is a smooth '''talker'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|That guy's a real '''talker'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Henry Alford|title=Future TED Talks|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2012/05/06/opinion/sunday/future-ted-talks.html|date=2012-05-05|archivedate=2012-05-09|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120509054938/https://www.nytimes.com/2012/05/06/opinion/sunday/future-ted-talks.html|passage=Returning TED '''talker''' Sherry Turkle, an author and academic, says that giving lectures about how lonely the Internet is making people has made her and her audiences even lonelier.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Eric Levenson|title=Alfred Newman, one of the last remaining Navajo Code Talkers, dies at 94|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2019/01/16/us/navajo-code-talker-alfred-newman-death-trnd/index.html|date=2019-01-16|passage=At Iwo Jima, code '''talkers''' passed over 800 error-free messages in a 48-hour period, according to the Congressional law honoring the program.}}
# Any creature or machine that talks.
#: {{ux|en|Some parrots are vociferous '''talkers'''.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|media}} A [[talk show]]
# {{lb|en|informal|media}} A talk-show host.
# {{lb|en|informal|media}} An all-talk radio station.
# {{lb|en|informal|media}} A popular topic of conversation.
#: {{ux|en|The royal engagement is likely to be a top '''talker''' right through the wedding.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|politics}} A [[talking point]].
# {{lb|en|Internet}} A stripped-down version of a [[MUD]] which is designed for talking, predating [[instant messenger]]s; a kind of early [[chat room]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[mouth|Mouth]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009 |title=The Power of the Dog: A Novel |author=Thomas Savage; Annie Proulx  |page= |ISBN= 0316082708|passage=Although on Sundays when the men had finished feeding cattle, the rest of the afternoon was free {{...}} still they weren't comfortable in the bunkhouse if George was abroad; he had a queer authority without even knowing it, an ability to upset you, maybe because he so seldom opened his '''talker''' and his silence made you look in upon yourself, on the guilt you always knew was there. }}
# {{lb|en|marketing}} A [[table talker]] or [[shelf-talker]].
# An augmentative and alternative communication device.

